    "tranche": "T6",
    "tranche_reason": "The paper measures detected concepts and concept diversity during vision-model training, but it does not test whether individual neurons respond to several unrelated inputs or any other listed claim version.",
    "gate_note": "The paper reports results about neuron-level concepts, interpretability counts, and concept-diversity metrics. Those results do not measure polysemanticity as defined by the claim versions; rows below are recorded as related findings, not as tests of a version. It also mentions prior work on multimodal neurons, but those cited results are not included as rows.",
    "test_reason": "Concept-Monitor assigns each neuron a single best-matching concept and tracks concept diversity across training; it never measures whether neurons respond to multiple unrelated inputs, nor any cause or rate of polysemanticity. The only mention is a passing remark (Fig 12 caption) that a top-concept-only description may be incomplete for polysemantic neurons, and a citation of Zoom In / multimodal neurons.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Mostly correct. The authors conclude that Concept-Monitor makes training transparent via neuron concepts, and that their diversity regularizer improves accuracy, interpretability and concept diversity. Note: the claimed interpretability gain holds only for ResNet-18; ResNet-50's count fell. The paper does not address polysemanticity beyond a single caption remark.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "The study proposes a concept-detection and embedding pipeline for tracking neuron concepts over training, plus a training regularizer. It does not reproduce the original sources’ neuron investigations or measure mixed unrelated inputs.",
    "method_sensitivity": "The paper reports that anchor-distance and embedding visualizations vary with temperature, and that interpretable-neuron counts vary with the threshold τ. It also reports differences across concept detectors in the Appendix.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "Concept Diversity Regularizer lowers anchor distance in ResNet-18 and ResNet-50. It raises the interpretable-neuron count in ResNet-18 (106 to 148) but lowers it in ResNet-50 (544 to 361).",
        "proposed_claim": "A concept-diversity regularizer changes single-concept interpretability counts, in model-dependent directions.",
